I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the request would send input text to an external host under an authority the graph doesn't declare. The approval isn't reflected in the graph definition yet, so I can't treat it as granted. The node below uses only `state-rw`.

It marks each considered id as seen by storing the run date under that key, and reports how many ids it recorded, so `recorded >= 0` holds trivially for the `u32`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in published.considered.iter() {
            state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

